    parentName: "ul"
  }, mdx("strong", {
    parentName: "li"
  }, "The Marketing Myth:"), " \"Nervous system regulation\" has mutated into a popular wellness marketing brand, often promising to cure complex emotional and structural issues through simplistic vagal stimulation exercises.")), mdx("p", null, "This creates a paradox: ", mdx("strong", {
    parentName: "p"
  }, "If the evolutionary narrative of Polyvagal Theory is scientifically flawed, why do somatic protocols (such as intense breathwork, cold exposure, and postural releases) yield such consistent, therapeutic results?")), mdx("p", null, "The answer is that the clinical maps of Polyvagal Theory are useful metaphors, but they mischaracterize the actual physiological territory. To build a grounded, resilient science of somatic medicine, we must move past speculative evolutionary stories and analyze the hard, bottom-up biophysical mechanisms of somatic release."), mdx("pre", null, mdx("code", {
    parentName: "pre"
  }, "                 THE SPECULATIVE BIOPHYSICAL PIPELINE\n\n                [Intense Rhythmic/Mystical Breathing]\n                                  \u2502\n                                  \u25BC\n      [Hyperventilation] \u2500\u2500> [Hypocapnia (Low Blood CO2)]\n                                  \u2502\n                                  \u25BC\n            [Respiratory Alkalosis (Elevated Blood pH)]\n                                  \u2502\n                                  \u25BC (The Bohr Effect)\n         [Cellular Hypoxia / Decreased Brain O2 Delivery]\n                                  \u2502\n         \u250C\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n         \u25BC                                                 \u25BC\n[Forced Cortical Muting]                        [Mechanical Hydraulics]\n- Mutes Prefrontal Cortex & DMN.                - Diaphragm maximal movement.\n- Top-down suppression collapses.               - Thoracic/abdominal pressure shifts.\n- Stored brainstem impulses escape.             - Connective tissue shears/releases.\n         \u2502                                                 \u2502\n         \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252C\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n                                  \u25BC\n                     [Somatic Release / Catharsis]\n")), mdx("hr", null), mdx("h2", {
    "id": "2-respiratory-chemistry-hypocapnia-and-alkalosis"
  }, "2. Respiratory Chemistry: Hypocapnia and Alkalosis"), mdx("p", null, "In intense somatic breath practices (such as Holotropic breathwork, Rebirthing, Wim Hof breathing, or ancient ", mdx("em", {
