    parentName: "ul"
  }, mdx("strong", {
    parentName: "li"
  }, "Altered Ionic Calcium Binding:"), " This alkaline shift alters the electrical charge of blood proteins, causing them to bind more readily to free calcium ions. The drop in ionized calcium destabilizes the resting membrane potential of peripheral nerve fibers, causing them to fire spontaneously. This spontaneous firing manifests physically as tingling in the extremities and temporary muscular contraction (tetany), mechanically squeezing the body's structural tissues.")), mdx("p", null, "This alkalizing shift introduces a massive systemic glitch into the peripheral nervous system, temporarily overriding the executive brain's fine-tuned control of the body."), mdx("hr", null), mdx("h2", {
